<article class="env-lemma" id="05P2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05P2">Lemma <span data-tag="05P2">28.21.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is a flat $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite presentation and for all $x \in X$ the stalk $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a free $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is a locally free, finite type $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module of finite type, for every $x \in X$ the stalk $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a free $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module, and the function 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \rho _\mathcal {F} : X \to \mathbf{Z}, \quad x \longmapsto \dim _{\kappa (x)} \mathcal{F}_ x \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}} \kappa (x)  \]
</div>
<p>
 is locally constant in the Zariski topology on $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma immediately reduces to the affine case. In this case the lemma is a reformulation of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a>. The translation uses Lemmas <a href="/tag/01PB" data-tag="01PB">28.17.1</a>, <a href="/tag/01PC" data-tag="01PC">28.17.2</a>, <a href="/tag/05P0" data-tag="05P0">28.20.1</a>, and <a href="/tag/05JM" data-tag="05JM">28.21.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>